wifi: brcmfmac: complete action frames sent without a dwell time

brcmf_p2p_tx_action_frame() waits for
BRCMF_E_ACTION_FRAME_OFF_CHAN_COMPLETE unless P2P discovery is listening
on the frame's channel. The firmware
only sends that event after an off-channel dwell: for an action frame
sent with a dwell time of 0 it reports BRCMF_E_ACTION_FRAME_COMPLETE
alone, so the driver waits until P2P_AF_MAX_WAIT_TIME (2 s) for every
such frame, and when the frame was not acknowledged it does not wake up
at all before the timeout.

Do not wait for the off-channel completion when there is no dwell
time, and complete the transmission on BRCMF_E_STATUS_NO_ACK as well
when no off-channel completion is expected.

P2P frames always carry a dwell time (brcmf_p2p_send_action_frame()
sets one), so they keep waiting for the off-channel completion.

Tool use: this change was prepared with the help of an AI coding
assistant (Claude), which read the driver, wrote the change and the
changelog, and ran the test described in the cover letter; the
submitter reviewed and tested it.

(Upstream series for wireless-next, carried in Splanc's Pi images: pi/provisioning/nix/brcmfmac-actframe.nix.)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/p2p.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/p2p.c
index f8e6cb4fa..ac5ecda6c 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/p2p.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/p2p.c
@@ -1547,6 +1547,8 @@ int brcmf_p2p_notify_action_tx_complete(struct brcmf_if *ifp,
 			 * WLC_E_ACTION_FRAME_OFFCHAN_COMPLETE event
 			 */
 			brcmf_p2p_stop_wait_next_action_frame(cfg);
+			if (!p2p->wait_for_offchan_complete)
+				complete(&p2p->send_af_done);
 		}
 
 	} else {
@@ -1574,6 +1576,7 @@ static s32 brcmf_p2p_tx_action_frame(struct brcmf_if *ifp,
 				     struct brcmf_fil_af_params_le *af_params)
 {
 	struct brcmf_pub *drvr = p2p->cfg->pub;
+	u32 listen_chan;
 	s32 err = 0;
 
 	brcmf_dbg(TRACE, "Enter\n");
@@ -1592,9 +1595,14 @@ static s32 brcmf_p2p_tx_action_frame(struct brcmf_if *ifp,
 	p2p->af_sent_channel = le32_to_cpu(af_params->channel);
 	p2p->af_tx_sent_jiffies = jiffies;
 
-	if (test_bit(BRCMF_P2P_STATUS_DISCOVER_LISTEN, &p2p->status) &&
-	    p2p->af_sent_channel ==
-	    ieee80211_frequency_to_channel(p2p->remain_on_channel.center_freq))
+	/* Without a dwell time the firmware sends no
+	 * BRCMF_E_ACTION_FRAME_OFF_CHAN_COMPLETE.
+	 */
+	listen_chan =
+		ieee80211_frequency_to_channel(p2p->remain_on_channel.center_freq);
+	if (!af_params->dwell_time ||
+	    (test_bit(BRCMF_P2P_STATUS_DISCOVER_LISTEN, &p2p->status) &&
+	     p2p->af_sent_channel == listen_chan))
 		p2p->wait_for_offchan_complete = false;
 	else
 		p2p->wait_for_offchan_complete = true;
